          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Which of the following reduces to a quadratic inequality?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{2x-3}\\geq2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\dfrac32$, multiply by $(2x-3)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-3&\\geq2(2x-3)^2\\\\2(2x-3)^2-(2x-3)&\\leq0\\\\8x^2-26x+21&\\leq0.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is quadratic.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x-3}{x+4}\\geq2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-4$, multiply by $(x+4)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-3)(x+4)&\\geq2(x+4)^2\\\\(2x-3)(x+4)-2(x+4)^2&\\geq0\\\\-11(x+4)&\\geq0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic terms cancel, leaving a linear inequality.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x+4}\\geq x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.\n\nThe taught denominator-square method produces a cubic inequality.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-4$, multiply by $(x+4)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+4&\\geq x(x+4)^2\\\\x(x+4)^2-(x+4)&\\leq0\\\\(x+4)(x^2+4x-1)&\\leq0\\\\x^3+8x^2+15x-4&\\leq0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe taught method produces a cubic inequality.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{2x-3}\\geq\\dfrac{1}{x+4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\dfrac32,-4$, multiply by $[(2x-3)(x+4)]^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-3)(x+4)^2&\\geq(2x-3)^2(x+4)\\\\(2x-3)(x+4)^2-(2x-3)^2(x+4)&\\geq0\\\\(7-x)(2x-3)(x+4)&\\geq0.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is cubic.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x-3}{x+4}\\geq\\dfrac{5-x}{3x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-4,-\\dfrac23$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x-3}{x+4}-\\frac{5-x}{3x+2}&\\geq0\\\\\\frac{(2x-3)(3x+2)-(5-x)(x+4)}{(x+4)(3x+2)}&\\geq0\\\\\\frac{7x^2-6x-26}{(x+4)(3x+2)}&\\geq0.\\end{align*}$$\nMultiplying by $[(x+4)(3x+2)]^2>0$ gives\n$$(7x^2-6x-26)(x+4)(3x+2)\\geq0,$$\nwhich is quartic.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{2x-3}+x+4\\geq2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\dfrac32$,\n$$\\frac{1}{2x-3}+x+2\\geq0.$$\nMultiply by $(2x-3)^2>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-3)+(x+2)(2x-3)^2&\\geq0\\\\(2x-3)[1+(x+2)(2x-3)]&\\geq0\\\\(2x-3)(2x^2+x-5)&\\geq0.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is cubic.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-task-9-15-part-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x-3}{x+4}+\\dfrac{5-x}{3x+2}\\geq2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-4,-\\dfrac23$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x-3}{x+4}+\\frac{5-x}{3x+2}-2&\\geq0\\\\\\frac{(2x-3)(3x+2)+(5-x)(x+4)-2(x+4)(3x+2)}{(x+4)(3x+2)}&\\geq0\\\\\\frac{-x^2-32x-2}{(x+4)(3x+2)}&\\geq0.\\end{align*}$$\nMultiplying by $[(x+4)(3x+2)]^2>0$ gives\n$$(-x^2-32x-2)(x+4)(3x+2)\\geq0,$$\nwhich is quartic.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
  },
